  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Stool Reducing Substance Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>No reducing substances are detected in the stool. It suggests normal digestion and absorption of carbohydrates in the gastrointestinal tract.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Positive</div></td><td><div>Reducing substances are detected in the stool. It indicates the presence of undigested carbohydrates in the stool, which may be due to conditions such as carbohydrate malabsorption, lactose intolerance, or certain gastrointestinal disorders. Further evaluation, including additional tests and clinical assessment, is needed to determine the underlying cause.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
